        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 92
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 20:5",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And I took my concubine, and cut her in pieces, and sent her throughout all the country of the inheritance of Israel: for they have committed lewdness and folly in Israel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 155,
            "end": 160,
            "text": "OR disgrace, wantonness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 20:6",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, ye are all children of Israel; give here your advice and counsel.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 14
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 20:7",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 20,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And all the people arose as one man, saying, We will not any of us go to his tent, neither will we any of us turn into his house.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 66
